<!--
    decbench: in a RUN of structurally identical assignment diamonds, kuna
    re-rolls only every other one.
      Case: O0-bash-bash-shell_initialize  (docs/decbench/triage/)

    On that case three source-identical call arguments
    (`privileged_mode||restricted||should_be_restricted||running_setuid`) come
    out as ONE re-rolled boolean assignment and TWO explicit
    `if (...) v = 1; else { v = 0; }` diamonds.  Scaling a chain of N identical
    diamonds, kuna recovers exactly ceil(N/2) of them (measured N = 1..8:
    1 1 2 2 3 3 4 4).

    Source of this testcase (gcc -O0 -fno-pie -fno-stack-protector -c), three
    identical constant-assignment diamonds in a row.  The indirect calls keep the
    object relocation-free and force the merged value onto a stack slot, so both
    arms of each diamond COPY a constant into the SAME storage (the shape
    `iteregion` matches):

        int t(int c, void (*g)(void), void (*f)(int))
        {
          int x;
          g(); if (c) x = 7; else x = 9; f(x);
          g(); if (c) x = 7; else x = 9; f(x);
          g(); if (c) x = 7; else x = 9; f(x);
          return x;
        }

    Root cause (P8, kuna's own passes).  `iteregion` and `iteboolean` share the
    leaf helper `leaf_bblock` (`p8_structure/kuna_iteregion.rs`), which descends a
    `BlockList` of ONE component but returns None for a list of two or more:

        BlockType::Ls | BlockType::Graph =>
            if blk.get_size() != 1 { return None; }

    The collapse structurer concatenates a just-collapsed predecessor together
    with the following condition block into a two-component `BlockList`, and that
    list becomes component 0 of the next `BlockIf`.  A chain of identical diamonds
    alternates between the two shapes, so every other one is declined, and which
    ones are missed depends on the NEIGHBOURING structure, not on the diamond
    itself.  Confirmed by instrumenting `match_ite_assignment` on this exact
    object: the folded diamonds report `cond_ty=Copy cbr=true`, the declined one
    `cond_ty=Ls cond_sz=2 cbr=false`, with both arms passing every other test.

    The fix (`option itecondlist on`, the default) descends a condition-position
    `BlockList` to its LAST component before the leaf test.  It is sound because
    the rewrite is print-only and the printer already renders that shape:
    `emit_block_if` emits the condition component once under NO_BRANCH (its
    statements) and once under ONLY_BRANCH (its branch), while `emit_block_ls`
    emits every component under NO_BRANCH but only the LAST under ONLY_BRANCH,
    so the leading components print as ordinary statements before the `if` header
    either way.  Restricted to `BlockList`: `emit_block_graph` ignores ONLY_BRANCH,
    so a `BlockGraph` is deliberately excluded.

    Stage model: P8 "goto-quality" (S8 structured-tree rewrite), rendered in P9.
    The P0 assertion `option itecondlist on|off` selects it; the pass is
    print-only (it widens which condition blocks `iteregion`/`iteboolean` accept,
    and mutates no p-code).

    Pass 1 (option itecondlist off) reproduces the gap: 2 of the 3 identical
    diamonds fold and the middle one stays an explicit `if (c) v1 = 7; else
    { v1 = 9; }`.
    Pass 2 (option itecondlist on, the default) proves the fix: all 3 fold, and
    the statements around them are unchanged.
-->
